        "title": {
          "zh": "第一幕 · 一条普通的街",
          "en": "An ordinary street"
        },
        "text": {
          "zh": "维米尔没有画教堂或广场，而是画了两栋普通的房子。这可能是北欧艺术中最早的普通房屋外观“肖像”。",
          "en": "Vermeer painted no church or square, just two ordinary houses. It may be the earliest \"portrait\" of an ordinary house exterior in northern European art."
        }
      },
      {
        "title": {
          "zh": "第二幕 · 一百年的谜",
          "en": "A century-old puzzle"
        },
        "text": {
          "zh": "近一个世纪以来，学者们一直在争论：这条街是真实存在，还是维米尔想象出来的？2015年，艺术史学家弗兰斯·格赖岑豪特查阅17世纪的码头登记册，发现全城只有一个地方有两个相邻的门道，和画中一样：弗拉明街40–42号。",
          "en": "For nearly a century, scholars debated whether this street was real or imagined. In 2015, art historian Frans Grijzenhout searched a 17th-century quay register and found only one place with two gateways side by side, just as in the painting: Vlamingstraat 40–42."
        }
      },
      {
        "title": {
          "zh": "第三幕 · 姑妈的家",
          "en": "His aunt's house"
        },
        "text": {
          "zh": "右边的房子属于维米尔守寡的姑妈。维米尔的母亲和姐姐就住在运河对面，这是他一定看过很多次的景色。",
          "en": "The house on the right belonged to Vermeer's widowed aunt. His mother and sister lived across the canal; it was a view he must have seen many times."
        }
      }
    ]
